---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Which digital marketing service should my business start with?",
    answer:
      "That depends on your market, current website, customer acquisition model, competition, budget and how quickly results are required. We prefer to assess those factors before recommending channels.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "How long does SEO take to produce results?",
    answer:
      "SEO is generally a medium- to long-term acquisition channel. Timing varies considerably based on competition, website condition, market authority, content quality and the searches being targeted.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can Google Ads generate leads immediately?",
    answer:
      "Paid search can generate visibility quickly once campaigns are active, but profitable lead generation still depends on targeting, competition, the offer, landing experience and conversion quality.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do you guarantee rankings or a specific number of leads?",
    answer:
      "No responsible marketing provider can guarantee a specific organic ranking or customer volume because search engines, auctions, competitors and customer behaviour are outside the provider's control. We focus on measurable work and continuous optimisation.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals handle both the website and marketing?",
    answer:
      "Yes. This can be particularly useful because technical performance, SEO, landing pages, analytics and conversion paths often need changes to the website itself.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do you work with businesses outside Sri Lanka?",
    answer:
      "Yes. LKProfessionals can support digital marketing requirements for businesses targeting local, national and international markets depending on the project scope.",
  },
];
---

<section class="marketing-faq">
  <div class="site-container marketing-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Digital marketing FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before spending time or budget on acquisition.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="marketing-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .marketing-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .marketing-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .marketing-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .marketing-faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .marketing-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .marketing-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .marketing-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .marketing-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .marketing-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
